&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grit &lt;/strong&gt;- You demonstrate grit by having the courage to commit and persevere. You’re committed, earnest, and dive in to get the job done well with a positive attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrity&lt;/strong&gt; - Simply put, do what you say and say what you&#39;ll do. You’re honest and forthright, have a strong moral compass, and strive to match your words with your actions while leading by example.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplicity&lt;/strong&gt; - Be like Einstein: “Everything should be made as simple as possible, but no simpler.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor (JD) or equivalent law degree and admitted to practice in at least one relevant jurisdiction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5+ years of substantive employment law experience, preferably including in-house experience, international employment counseling, EOR, PEO, global mobility, HR technology, or other cross-border employment operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience advising on employee lifecycle matters, including complex terminations, performance management, leave, employee relations, employment documentation, recurring compliance, and dispute risk across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting an EOR business, global employment platform, international HR operations, or multi-country employment counseling is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build legal standards, risk frameworks, escalation paths, playbooks, policies, knowledge bases, and SOPs that enable non-legal teams to operate with consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how employment-law requirements should be translated into operational workflows, product requirements, customer guidance, and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment in managing legal, operational, customer, employee, financial, and reputational risk in sensitive employment matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain complex legal concepts to non-legal stakeholders in a practical and concise way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cross-functionally and influence stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated time management, organizational, and analytical skills, including the ability to manage multiple complex matters across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing outside counsel and obtaining practical, cost-effective legal advice across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English; proficiency in another relevant language is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Occasional travel is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The base wage range for this position is targeted at 98,000-127,000 EUR per year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
